      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The transcriptional repressor Id2 is constitutively expressed in all innate lymphoid cells (ILCs) and is required for their development. In this issue of Immunity, Mowel et al. (2017) demonstrate that Id2 expression is regulated by a cell type-specific cis-regulatory element in group 1 ILCs that is demarcated by a long non-coding RNA."
      },
